BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Threads Tell Stories: How Archaeologists Read Andean Textiles
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261104T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261104T130000
DTSTAMP:20261024T122928Z
UID:aa0d77ab82d552610d4150442d862409@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nWhat can a piece of clo
 th tell us about the people who made and used it? Using contemporary Andea
 n textiles\, alongside images from archaeological research\, visitors will
  be encouraged to look closely at fibers\, threads\, weaving techniques\, 
 colors\, and patterns and discuss how these details can help archaeologist
 s understand technology\, identity\, labor\, and everyday life in the past
 . Become a “textile detective” as you consider what clues different ma
 terials and manufacturing choices can provide about the people and communi
 ties that produced them. Presented by Rosa María Varillas\, PhD Candidate
  in Anthropology\, University of Illinois Chicago\; Scientific Affiliate\,
  Field Museum.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet
 -a-scientist/threads-tell-stories-how-archaeologists-read-andean-textiles
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/threads-tell-s
 tories-how-archaeologists-read-andean-textiles
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Threads Tell Stories: How Archaeologists Read Andean
  Textile
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: Threads Tell Stories: How Archaeologists Read Ande
 an Textile
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Armour Seminar: Megan Baker
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261104T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261104T130000
DTSTAMP:20261024T122928Z
UID:d1323effbfe0addef946fbd36a16516c@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,museum_professional,community_scientist,r
 esearcher,adults
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: 
 General\\n\\nJoin us for a talk by Megan Baker\, Northwestern University. 
 This session will take place in the Founders' Room on the main level. The 
 A. Watson Armour III Seminar Series is a weekly seminar highlighting the r
 esearch of science professionals across a broad spectrum of scientific int
 erests\, disciplines\, and lived experiences. This series connects the Fie
 ld Museum’s research\, collections\, conservation\, and associated commu
 nity with professionals at the forefront of life\, geophysical\, and socia
 l sciences. Lectures are open to the public and regularly highlight or com
 plement research conducted by Field Museum staff and affiliates. Have a sp
 eaker to suggest? Contact us at armourseminars@fieldmuseum.org.\\n\\nMore 
 info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/a-watson-armour-iii-research-
 seminar-series/armour-seminar-megan-baker
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/a-watson-armour-iii-research-se
 minar-series/armour-seminar-megan-baker
