BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tlingit Artist James Johnson: Haa Shagoon—The Path Forward
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261110T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261110T190000
DTSTAMP:20261024T122928Z
UID:a1bf775c6eedc59be03426f8e9f5d56d@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nAs part of Native American He
 ritage Month\, join us for an evening conversation with James Johnson. Jam
 es will discuss his artistic practice\, the importance of preserving tradi
 tional Tlingit ways of creating\, and how he draws on the knowledge and wo
 rk of his ancestors in his contemporary practice. James Johnson is an awar
 d-winning Tlingit Artist and Carver\, born and raised in Juneau\, AK. He b
 elongs to the Tlingit Ch’áak’ Dakl’aweidi Clan (Eagle Killerwhale).
  James is a multi-disciplinary artist but specializes in Tlingit formline 
 design\, with a focus on traditional wood carving. Carving is an integral 
 part of the preservation of Tlingit history and culture. “Carving is our
  visual language that represents who the Tlingit people are\, and how we l
 ive in balance with all things.” James’s contemporary practice builds 
 upon an indigenous artistic continuum while honoring the culture and its r
 ich traditions. This event takes place on a Legendary Late Hours day and i
 s included with admission. The event takes place in the Montgomery Ward Le
 cture Hall\, on the lower level.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.o
 rg/our-events/cultural-programming/tlingit-artist-james-johnson-haa-shagoo
 nthe-path-forward
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/cultural-programming/tlingit-ar
 tist-james-johnson-haa-shagoonthe-path-forward
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Tlingit Artist James Johnson: Haa Shagoon—The Path
  Forward
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: Tlingit Artist James Johnson: Haa Shagoon—The Pa
 th Forward
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
