BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mongolian Fossil Plants
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261118T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261118T130000
DTSTAMP:20261024T122928Z
UID:0052681a69feabb6bd409fa5cf386c7f@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nCome join Fabiani Herrera\, N
 egaunee Associate Curator of Paleobotany\, as he reveals the mysteries beh
 ind 120-million-year-old fossilized plants from Mongolia through the use o
 f a Scanning Electron Microscope. Examine different parts of these fossil 
 plants under the Scanning Electron Microscope and Wentzscope to reveal the
  tiny secrets that shaped the Age of Dinosaurs and beyond! Discover the ch
 aracteristics of these ancient plants that connect them to some of their m
 odern relatives and help scientists map their evolutionary lineage.\\n\\nM
 ore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/mongolia
 n-fossil-plants
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/mongolian-foss
 il-plants
